<title>GERMANY: GERMAN JULY M3 UP ANNUALISED 5.7 PCT VS Q4 96.</title>
<headline>GERMAN JULY M3 UP ANNUALISED 5.7 PCT VS Q4 96.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank gave the</p>
<p>following data on Tuesday for German July M3 money supply</p>
<p>growth.</p>
<p>						 June 97	  June 97</p>
<p> Annualised vs average Q4 1996	 5.7		6.4 pct</p>
<p> Non-annualised vs average Q4 1996   3.8		3.7 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - The Bundesbank's target range for 1997 M3 money</p>
<p>supply growth is 3-1/2 to 6-1/2 percent. Economists polled by</p>
<p>Reuters on average predicted M3 growth would slow to 6.3</p>
<p>percent against the fourth quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
